{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 33, :comments ["<b>And her discharge in her impurity.</b> For דָּוָה (her menstruation) indicates that this came about because of sin, and therefore she is impure." "<b>And the zav.</b> The point regarding the matter of the zav is to give warning concerning a sin that preceded." "<b>Her discharge, for the male and for the female.</b> And along with this, it is fitting to consider the distinction between the discharge of the male and the discharge of the female: the discharge of the female does not defile except what is reddish (אָדֹם), while the discharge of the male does not defile except when it is not reddish." "<b>And for a man who lies with an impure woman.</b> It is also fitting to consider that regarding the man who lies with an impure woman it says וְתָהִי נִדָּתָהּ עָלָיו (Leviticus 15:24), and it does not say thus regarding a pure woman whom the zav lies with. For this indicates that the male is more corrupted by lying with the menstruating woman than the woman is corrupted by lying with the sick man, as experience demonstrates in leprosy and similar cases."], :book :leviticus, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 15, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:36:24.800440023Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}